# Transactions

> Status: Ready
> Priority: P0
> Depends On: Accounts, Categories
> Next Feature: Budgets

---

# Overview

Transactions are the core records of income and expense in Kin Finance.

Every Transaction records a financial event: money coming in (income) or going out (expense). Transactions are linked to an Account and a Category.

In MVP, Transactions are simple (no split, no recurring). Both Owner and Member can create, edit, and delete Transactions freely. Every Transaction records who created and updated it.

---

# Goals

- Allow users to record income and expenses.
- Auto-update Account balance on every transaction change.
- Track who created and updated each Transaction.

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- Create a Transaction (income or expense).
- Edit a Transaction.
- Delete a Transaction.
- List Transactions with date filtering.
- Auto-update Account balance on create/edit/delete.
- Record createdBy and updatedBy metadata.

## Out of Scope

- Split transactions (future).
- Recurring transactions (future).
- Attachments/receipts (future).
- Transfer between accounts (future).
- Multi-currency (future).

